          "source_text_sha256": "de11cd78f281b94546bec861a44e8b34213f873ca3859168574d04e143919db3",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: From June 2014 to December 2015, an individual regularly observed the sky with binoculars and a telescope, reporting several sightings of colored spheres, only visible on clear nights. The multi-colored spheres move slightly. The witness, in particular, recounts a lengthy observation on June 6, 2014. No other testimonies were collected. The long (30 minutes) and repeated observation of glowing points in the sky, moving slowly, appearing multicolored when viewed with binoculars or an astronomical telescope, suggests the observation of stars, particularly bright at low elevation. Given the sky map from the time of the observation, it could be Capella, Vega, or Deneb. The effect observed by the witness may be the result of an incorrect setting on the astronomical telescope. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of particularly bright stars at low elevation.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "0e8496311747d571e58f60abbde2e104d9bb7ac1aed0971498dc3896408055ad"
        }
